      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_6809808" metaid="metaid_1800" name="ECI2 isomerizes 3Z-enoyl-CoA to 2E-enoyl-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">ECI2 in the peroxisome matrix catalyzes the isomerizeation of 3Z-enoyl-CoA to 2E-enoyl-CoA. The active form of the enzyme is a homotrimer (Onwukwe et al. 2015). The reaction annotated here, involving octenoyl-CoA isomers is the one originally characterized by Geisbrecht et al. (1999), although the enzyme is active on enoyl-CoAs of a range of chain lengths.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
