      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2161794" metaid="metaid_1805" name="Arachidonate is converted to HXA3/B3 by ALOX12" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Arachidonate 12-lipoxygenase, 12S-type (ALOX12) converts arachidonate to both hepoxilin A3 (HXA3) and B3 (HXB3). They both incorporate an epoxide across the C-11 and C-12 double bond, as well as an additional hydroxyl moiety with HXA3 having a C-8 hydroxyl, whereas the HXB3 hydroxyl occurs at C-10 (Sutherland et al. 2001, Nigam et al. 2004).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
