      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9018877" metaid="metaid_1809" name="LTA4H:Zn2+ hydrolyses 5S,6S-epoxy-18(R)-HEPE to 18(R)-RvE1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Leukotriene A4 hydrolase (LTA4H) is a monomeric, soluble enzyme that uses a Zn2+ cofactor to catalyse the hydrolysis of the allylic epoxide leukotriene A4 (LTA4) (McGee and Fitzpatrick 1985). LTA4H can also catalyse the hydrolysis of 5S,6S-epoxy-18(R)-HEPE to the 18(R) stereoisomer of resolvin E1 (18(R)-RvE1) (Oh et al. 2011). The E-resolvins are antiinflammatory, pro-resolving, and non-phlogistic (that is, they mediate the clearance of leukocytes without eliciting an inflammatory response) (Serhan et al. 2008).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
