      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_389639" metaid="metaid_1811" name="phytanoyl-CoA + 2-oxoglutarate + O2 =&gt; 2-hydroxyphytanoyl-CoA + succinate + CO2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Peroxisomal phytanoyl-CoA dioxygenase catalyzes the reaction of phytanoyl-CoA, 2-oxoglutarate, and O2 to form 2-hydroxyphytanoyl-CoA, succinate, and CO2. The mature form of the enzyme lacks the first 30 amino acid residues of the full-length polypeptide and is complexed with Fe++. Mutations in this enzyme are the commonest cause of Refsum disease (Mukherji et al. 2001; McDonough et al. 2005).</p>
        </notes>
