      <reaction compartment="compartment_70616" fast="false" id="reaction_1482745" metaid="metaid_1813" name="PG is hydrolyzed to 1-acyl LPG by PLA2G4B (IM)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the inner mitochondrial membrane (IM), phosphatidylglycerol (PG) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by phospholipase A2 beta (PLA2G4B) to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidylglycerol (LPG) (Ghomashchi et al. 2010, Singer et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
