      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_266072" metaid="metaid_1838" name="LTA4 is hydolysed to LTB4 by LTA4H" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Leukotriene A4 hydrolase (LTA4H) is a monomeric, soluble enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of the allylic epoxide leukotriene A4 (LTA4) to the dihydroxy acid leukotriene B4 (LTB4) (Radmark et al. 1984, McGee and Fitzpatrick 1985).</p>
        </notes>
