      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_8868402" metaid="metaid_1839" name="OSBP exchanges 25OH-CHOL with PI4P from ER membrane to Golgi membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Oxysterol-binding protein 1 (OSBP) is involved in lipid countertransport between the Golgi and the ER membranes. It specifically exchanges sterols such as 25-hydroxycholesterol (25OH-CHOL) with phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate (PI4P), delivering it to the Golgi in exchange for PI4P, which is degraded by the SAC1/SACM1L phosphatases in the ER. The PH-FFAT region of OSBP is necessary for membrane tethering, which then directs forward sterol and backward PI4P transport by the ORD domain of OSBP (Mesmin et al. 2013).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
