      <reaction compartment="compartment_17947" fast="false" id="reaction_6809810" metaid="metaid_1845" name="PECR reduces 2E-phytenoyl-CoA to phytanoyl-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">PECR associated with the peroxisomal membrane catalyzes the NADPH-dependent reduction of 2E-phytenoyl-CoA to form phytanoyl-CoA (Das et al. 2000; Gloerich et al. 2006). The active form of the enzyme is inferred to be a homotetramer from unpublished data deposited in PDB (accession 1YXM). This reaction is part of the process by which dietary phytol, ultimately derived from chlorophyll, is catabolized (Van Veldhoven 2010).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
