      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_1606288" metaid="metaid_1848" name="SMPD4 hydrolyzes sphingomyelin (ER membrane)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">ER membrane-bound sphingomyelin phosphodiesterase 4 (SMPD4) hydrolyses sphingomyelin to ceramide (Krut et al. 2006). Loss-of-function mutations in the SMPD4 gene cause neurodevelopmental disorder with microcephaly, arthrogryposis, and structural brain anomalies (NEDMABA) (Magini et al., 2019).</p>
        </notes>
