      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_140355" metaid="metaid_1863" name="Arachidonate is oxidised to PGG2 by PTGS1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Prostaglandin G/H synthase PTGS1 exhibits a dual catalytic activity, a cyclooxygenase and a peroxidase. The cyclooxygenase function catalyzes the initial conversion of arachidonate to an intermediate, prostaglandin G2 (PGG2) (Hamberg et al. 1974, Nugteren 1973).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
