      <reaction compartment="compartment_13977" fast="false" id="reaction_6808464" metaid="metaid_1874" name="ALDH3B2 oxidises HXAL to PALM" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">ALDH3B2 (aldehyde dehydrogenase family 3 member B2), associated with cytosolic lipid droplets, catalyzes the NAD-dependent oxdidation of HXAL (hexadecanal) to PALM (palmitate). A geranylgeranylated cysteine residue mediates the enzyme's association with the lipid droplet (Kitamura et al. 2013, 2015).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
