      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9031896" metaid="metaid_1883" name="PD1n-3, PD2n-3 translocate from cytosol to extracellular region" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">To produce their pro-resolving effects, DPAn-3 derived protectins (PD1n-3 and PD2n-3) are released into the exudate of local inflammation sites (Dalli et al. 2013, Vik et al. 2017). The mechanism of translocation is unknown.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
