      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9018901" metaid="metaid_1891" name="5-HEDH dehydrogenates 5(S)-Hp-18(R)-HEPE to 18(R)-RvE2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">An unknown dehydrogenase reduces 5(S)-hydroperoxy-18(R)-hydroxyeicosapentaenoic acid (5(S)-Hp-18(R)-HEPE) into the 18(R) stereoisomer of resolvin E2 (18(R)-RvE2). The unknown enzyme may be 5-hydroxyeicosanoid dehydrogenase (5-HEDH) or one similar to this (Patel et al. 2009). Human neutrophils biosynthesise RvE2 in greater amounts than RvE1, suggesting a significant role for RvE2 (Tjonahen et al. 2006, Oh et al. 2012).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
