      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_209868" metaid="metaid_1896" name="CYP27B1 hydroxylates 25(OH)D to 1,25(OH)2D" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The second step in vitamin D activation requires hydroxylation of 25-hydroxyvitamin D (calcidiol, 25(OH)D) to 1-alpha, 25-dihydroxyvitamin D (1,25(OH)2D). This conversion is mediated by 25-hydroxyvitamin D-1-alpha hydroxylase (CYP27B1), an outer mitochondrial membrane-resident protein (Zehnder et al. 2002, Fritsche et al. 2003, Sawada et al. 1999).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
