      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_389889" metaid="metaid_1897" name="ACOX2:FAD, ACOXL:FAD oxidise (2S)-pristanoyl-CoA to trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In human liver and kidney tissue, monomeric peroxisomal ACOX2 (bound to FAD cofactor) catalyzes the reaction of (2S)-pristanoyl-CoA and O2 to form trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA and H2O2 (Vanhove et al. 1993; Baumgart et al. 1996). A putative acyl-coenzyme A oxidase-like protein ACOXL could catalyse this type of reaction but its activity has not yet been determined.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
