      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1675813" metaid="metaid_1914" name="PI is phosphorylated to PI4P by PI4KA/2B at the ER membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase alpha (PI4KA) (Wong et al. 1997, Gehrmann et al. 1999) or phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase type 2-beta (PI4K2B) (Wei et al. 2002) phosphorylate phosphatidylinositol (PI) to produce phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate (PI4P).</p>
        </notes>
