      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_350147" metaid="metaid_1928" name="VD3 translocates from extracellular region to ER membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Once vitamin D3 (VD3) is released from vitamin D binding protein (GC, DBP), it translocates from the extracellular region to the ER membrane, becoming available for hydroxylation by the microsomal enzyme CYP2R1 (Shinkyo et al. 2004).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
