      <reaction compartment="compartment_17906" fast="false" id="reaction_1483099" metaid="metaid_1936" name="PA translocates from the outer to the inner mitochondrial membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Phosphatidic acid (PA) transport within the mitochondrion occurs as free diffusion through the aqueous phase and not mediated by phospholipid transfer proteins. This event is inferred from rats (Chakraborty et al. 1999, Wojtczak et al. 1990).</p>
        </notes>
