      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482679" metaid="metaid_2000" name="PA is hydrolysed to 1-acyl LPA by PLA2G2A" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidic acid (PA) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by membrane-associated phospholipase A2 gamma 2A (PLA2G2A), to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) (Singer et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
