      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9020277" metaid="metaid_2001" name="ALOX5 dehydrogenates 4(S)-Hp-17(S)-HDHA to 4S(5)-epoxy-17(S)-HDHA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">5-lipoxygenase (ALOX5) possesses dual lipoxygenase activity (Shimizu et al. 1984). In polymorphonuclear (PMN) cells, ALOX5 can epoxygenate (via dehydration) 4(S)-hydroperoxy-17(S)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (4(S)-Hp-17(S)-HDHA) to form 4S(5)-epoxy-17(S)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (4S(5)-epoxy-17(S)-HDHA (Serhan et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
