      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9028263" metaid="metaid_2008" name="PGJ3 isomerises to δ12-PGJ3" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">It is proposed that prostaglandin J3 (PGJ3) isomerises to prostaglandin δ12-PGJ3 (δ12-PGJ3) (Fitzpatrick et al. 1983, Shibata et al. 2002). EPA supplementation to mice resulted in enhanced endogenous production of δ12-PGJ3, which was found to possess chemoprotective activity against myleoid leukemia, ablating leukemia stem cells in mice (Hegde et al. 2011, Finch et al. 2015).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
