      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9031807" metaid="metaid_2025" name="Protectins translocate from cytosol to extracellular region" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">To produce their pro-resolving effects, protectins PDX, (N)PD1, AT-(N)PD1 and 22-OH-(N)PD1 are released into the exudate of local inflammation sites (Serhan et al. 2014, 2015). The mechanism of translocation is unknown.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
