      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9026918" metaid="metaid_2040" name="Lipoxygenase oxidises 17(S)-Hp-DHA to 7(S),17(S)-diHp-DHA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In an alternative route to PCTR production, 17(S)-hydroperoxy-docosahexaenoic acid (17(S)-Hp-DHA) can undergo a second lipoxygenation at carbon 7 position to yield 7S,17S-dihydroperoxy-docosahexaenoic acid (7(S),17(S)-diHp-DHA). A lipoxygenase mediates this reaction although the exact human enzyme is unknown (Dalli et al. 2015).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
