      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_2161890" metaid="metaid_2055" name="Arachidonate is epoxidated to 5,6-EET by CYP(4)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Several cytochrome P450s (CYPs) convert arachidonate to 5,6-epoxyeicosatrienoic acid (5,6-EET). The CYPs and their references are as follows: CYP1A1, CYP1A2, CYP1B1 (Choudhary et al. 2004); CYP2J2 (Wu et al. 1996).</p>
        </notes>
