      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9024983" metaid="metaid_2066" name="ALOX12:Fe2+ dehydrogenates 14(S)-Hp-DHA to 13(S),14(S)-epoxy-DHA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In macrophages, lipoxygenase 12 (ALOX12:Fe2+) may abstract hydrogen from 14(S)-hydroperoxy-docosaheaenoic acid (14(S)-Hp-DHA) to form 13(S),14(S)-epoxy-DHA (Serhan et al. 2009, Dalli et al. 2013, Deng et al. 2014). This epoxy product is a central intermediate in maresin MaR1 and MaR2 and maresin conjugates in tissue regeneration (MCTR) biosyntheses (Dalli et al. 2016) as well as possessing potent proresolving activity (Dalli et al 2013).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
