      <reaction compartment="compartment_20699" fast="false" id="reaction_9851347" metaid="metaid_2090" name="B4GALT5/6 transfer Gal to GlcCer" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Beta-1,4-galactosyltransferases 5 and 6 (B4GALT5/6) catalyze the transfer of galactose from UDP-α-D-galactose onto glucosylceramide (GlcCer) to produce lactosylceramide (LacCer). LacCer is the primary precursor in the biosynthesis of complex glycosphingolipids (Tokuda et al., 2013; Yamaji and Hanada, 2014; reviewed by Chatterjee et al., 2021).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
