      <reaction compartment="compartment_5460" fast="false" id="reaction_8957389" metaid="metaid_2091" name="RPP14 (HTD2) dehydrates 3HA-CoA to t2E-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Polycistronic transcripts, where a single mRNA can encode several different polypeptide chains, are common in prokaryotes. In humans, only 3 bicistronic transcripts have been characterised to date. Human cDNAs encoding both RPP14 of the RNase P complex and mitochondrial 3-hydroxyacyl thioester dehydratase (HTD2) have been isolated. HTD2 functions in the mitochondrial fatty acid synthesis (FAS) pathway, dehydrating (3R)-hydroxyacyl-CoA (3HA-CoA) to trans-2-enoyl-CoA (t2E-CoA) (Autio et al. 2008).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
