      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_6810474" metaid="metaid_2098" name="NUDT19 hydrolyses acyl-CoA to 3',5'-ADP and acyl-PPANT" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Coenzyme A (CoA-SH) and acyl-coenzyme A (acyl-CoA) can be degraded in peroxisomes by two members of the Nudix (nucleoside diphosphates linked to some moiety X) hydrolase superfamily; NUDT7 and NUDT19. NUDT19 hydrolyses free fatty acyl-CoA to form acyl-phosphopantetheine (acyl-PPANT) and 3′,5′-ADP. Human NUDT19 activity is inferred from mouse Nudt19 activity (Ofman et al. 2006).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
