      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9026405" metaid="metaid_2099" name="ALOX5 oxidises 13(R)-HDPAn-3 to RvT1-4" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In neutrophils, 5-lipoxygenase (ALOX5) oxidises 13(R)-hydroxy-docosapentaenoic acid (13(R)-DPAn-3) to the 13(R)-resolvins RvT1-4 (7,13,20-trihydroxy-docosapentaenoic acid, 7,12,13-trihydroxy-docosapentaenoic acid, 7,8,13-trihydroxy-docosapentaenoic acid and 7,13-dihydroxy-docosapentaenoic acid respectively) (Dalli et al. 2015, Primdahl et al. 2016). They were all shown to posses anti-inflammatory and proresolving activities (Dalli et al. 2015). Recently, RvTs have been shown to mediate the proresolving actions of several statins in mice with inflammatory arthritis (Walker et al. 2017).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
