      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_443894" metaid="metaid_2102" name="TXA2 is hydrolysed to TXB2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Thromboxane A2 (TXA2) contains an unstable ether linkage that is rapidly hydrolysed under aqueous conditions to form the biologically inert thromboxane B2 (TXB2) (Wang et al. 2001, Hamberg et al. 1975), which is excreted.</p>
        </notes>
