      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9843721" metaid="metaid_2104" name="ABCC1,ABCG2 transport C18-S1P to extracellular region" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The proton pumps ABCC1, ABCG2 transport sphing-4-enine 1-phosphate (sphingosine-1-phosphate, C18-S1P) out of cells. ABCC1 is mainly expressed in mast cells, fibroblasts, and endothelial cells (Mitra et al., 2006; Nieuwenhuis et al., 2009). Export of C18-S1P by ABCG2 has been shown in MCF-7 epithelial cells (Takabe et al., 2010). These processes support a role of C18-S1P secretion in mast cell migration, cytoprotection, maintenance of epithelial barriers, and cancer/multidrug resistance (reviewed by Reitsema et al., 2014).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
