      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_8848339" metaid="metaid_2111" name="PNPLA5 hydrolyzes TAG" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">PNPLA5 (patatin-like phospholipase domain-containing protein 5, also known as GS2 like) catalyzes the hydrolysis of TAG (triacylglycerol) to DAG (diacylglycerol) and one molecule of LCFA (long chain fatty acid) (Gao and Simon 2007).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
