      <reaction compartment="compartment_161320" fast="false" id="reaction_9842115" metaid="metaid_2114" name="PSAP(195-273) dimer binds PE" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">By encapsulating phosphatidylethanolamines (PE) of different sizes from the membrane of intralysosomal luminal vesicles (ILV), the Saposin B (PSAP(195-273) dimer can solubilize relatively large lipid ligands from these membranes (Ahn et al., 2003).</p>
        </notes>
