      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_209754" metaid="metaid_2130" name="Photolytic cleavage and thermal isomerization of 7-dehydroCHOL" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The skin's exposure to UV rays from sunlight induces the photolytic cleavage of 7-dehydrocholesterol to previtamin D3. This is followed by thermal isomerization to form vitamin D3 (VD3, cholecalciferol) (Holick et al. 1977).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
