      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482811" metaid="metaid_2136" name="DAG is hydrolyzed to 2-MAG by PNPLA2/3" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, patatin-like phospholipase domain-containing proteins 2/3 (PNPLA2/3) hydrolyze diacylglycerol (DAG), removing an acyl group to form 2-monoacylglycerol (2-MAG) (He et al. 2010, Jenkins et al. 2004, Basantani et al. 2011).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
