      <reaction compartment="compartment_17906" fast="false" id="reaction_1482548" metaid="metaid_2138" name="1-acyl LPA is acylated to PA by AGPAT5 (OM)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the outer mitochondrial (OM) membrane, 1-acyl lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) is acylated to phosphatidic acid (PA) by the enzyme 1-acyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferases epsilon (AGPAT5) (Prasad et al. 2011).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
