      <reaction compartment="compartment_17906" fast="false" id="reaction_1482604" metaid="metaid_2144" name="PA is hydrolyzed to 1-acyl LPA by PLA2[1] (OM)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the outer mitochondrial (OM) membrane, phosphatidic acid (PA) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by phospholipase A2 alpha/beta/delta/zeta (PLA2G4A/B/D/F) to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) (Ghomashchi et al. 2010).</p>
        </notes>
