      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9026927" metaid="metaid_2149" name="GGT hydrolyses RCTR1 to RCTR2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Presumably following a similar synthesis route to protectin conjugate in tissue regeneration 2 (PCTR2), resolvin conjugate in tissue regeneration 1 (RCTR1) could be hydrolysed to RCTR2 (8-cysteinylglycinyl, 7,17-dihydroxy-docosahexaenoic acid) by the actions of a glutathione transferase (GGT) (Dalli et al. 2015).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
