      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482907" metaid="metaid_2166" name="PG is hydrolyzed to 1-acyl LPG by PLA2G2A" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidylglycerol (PG) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by membrane-associated phospholipase A2 gamma 2A, PLA2G2A (Singer et al. 2002), to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidylglycerol (LPG).</p>
        </notes>
