      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9018868" metaid="metaid_2184" name="GPX4-2 reduces 18(S)-HpEPE to 18(S)-HEPE" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In PMNs, cytosolic phospholipid hydroperoxide glutathione peroxidase (GPX4 isoform 2, GPX4-2) (Yagi et al. 1996) is a likely candidate for the reduction of organic hydroperoxides such as 18(S)-HpEPE to 18(S)-hydroxyeicosapentaenoic acid (18(S)-HEPE) (Han et al. 2013) using glutathione (GSH) as an electron donor (Brigelius-Flohe and Maiorino 2013).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
