      <reaction compartment="compartment_70616" fast="false" id="reaction_1482847" metaid="metaid_2187" name="PG is hydrolysed to 2-acyl LPG by PLA2G4B (IM)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the inner mitochondrial (IR) membrane, phosphatidylglycerol (PG) is hydrolysed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by phospholipase A2 beta (PLA2G4B) (Ghomashchi et al. 2010) to form 2-acyl lysophosphatidylglycerol (LPG). Phospholipase A2 enzymes show not only PLA2 hydrolysing activity to form the 1-acyl lysophospholipid but also have a degree of PLA1 activity, producing a 2-acyl lysophospholipid.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
