      <reaction compartment="compartment_984" fast="false" id="reaction_428690" metaid="metaid_2190" name="PLPP1 dephosphorylates extracellular sphingosine-1-phosphate" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Phospholipid phosphatase 2 (PLPP2, PPAP2A, LPP3) enzyme associated with the plasma membrane catalyzes the hydrolysis of extracellular sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P) to form sphingosine and orthophosphate. The reaction is essential for removing S1P from plasma and cell uptake of sphingosine (Roberts et al., 1998; Zhao et al., 2007; reviewed by Tang et al., 2015).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
