      <reaction compartment="compartment_20699" fast="false" id="reaction_1675928" metaid="metaid_2195" name="PI4P is phosphorylated to PI(3,4)P2 by PIK3C2A/G at the Golgi membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the Golgi membrane, phosphatidylinositol-4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit alpha (PIK3C2A) (Domin et al. 2000, Arcaro et al. 2000) and phosphatidylinositol-4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit gamma (PIK3C2G) (Ono et al. 1998, Rozycka et al. 1998, Misawa et al. 1998) phosphorylate phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate (PI4P) to phosphatidylinositol 3,4-bisphosphate (PI(3,4)P2). PIK3C2G phosphorylates phosphatidylinositol (PI) and PI4P but not phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate (PI(4,5)P2).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
