      <reaction compartment="compartment_984" fast="false" id="reaction_9733960" metaid="metaid_2200" name="Bile salts and acids dissociate from ALB" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Bile salts and acids exist in the blood as complexes with serum albumin (ALB) (Rudman and Kendall 1957, Roda et al. 1982), and their uptake by hepatocytes must involve disruption of this complex, but the molecular mechanism coupling release of a bile salt or acid from ALB is unknown.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
