      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9020256" metaid="metaid_2203" name="ALOX5 dehydrogenates 7(S)-Hp-17R-HDHA to 7S(8)-epoxy-17R-HDHA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">5-lipoxygenase (ALOX5) possesses dual lipoxygenase activity (Shimizu et al. 1984). In polymorphonuclear (PMN) cells, ALOX5 can epoxygenate (via dehydration) 7(S)-hydroperoxy-17(R)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (7(S)-Hp-17(R)-HDHA) to form 7S(8)-epoxy-17(R)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (7S(8)-epoxy-17(R)-HDHA (Serhan et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
