      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_163568" metaid="metaid_2209" name="phosphorylated perilipin + H2O -&gt; perilipin + orthophosphate" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Rat perilipin is dephosphorylated by protein phosphatase 1 (Clifford et al. 1998). All three protein phosphatase 1 isoforms appear competent to carry out this reaction and there are no data to indicate which one preferentially acts on perilipin in vivo. Dephosphorylation of human perilipin has not been studied in detail, so the human reaction is inferred from the well-studied rat one.</p>
        </notes>
