      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_9947207" metaid="metaid_2233" name="MSMO1 oxidizes 4a-me-5a-cholest-8-en-3b-ol to 4a-carboxy-5a-cholest-8-ene-3b-ol" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">MSMO1 (Methylsterol monooxygenase 1), associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane, oxidizes 4a-me-5a-cholest-8-en-3b-ol to 4a-carboxy-5a-cholest-8-en-3b-ol. Evidence for this function of human MSMO1 protein is indirect, coming from studies of steroid synthesis intermediates accumulated in patients with defects in the enzyme (He et al. 2011).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
