      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482777" metaid="metaid_2236" name="TAG is hydrolyzed to DAG by PNPLA2/3" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, triacylglycerol (TAG) is hydrolyzed, removing one of its acyl groups to form diacylglycerol (DAG) by patatin-like phospholipase domain-containing protein 2/3 (PNPLA2/3) (He et al. 2010, Jenkins et al. 2004, Basantani et al. 2011).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
