      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_193816" metaid="metaid_2266" name="Cholest-5-ene-3beta,7alpha,27-triol is oxidized and isomerized to 4-cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Cholest-5-ene-3beta,7alpha,27-triol and NAD+ react to form 4-cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one and NADH + H+, in a reaction catalyzed by HSD3B7 (3 beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase type 7) in the endoplasmic reticulum membrane. Its function in vivo has been confirmed in studies of patients with defects in bile acid synthesis (Schwarz et al. 2000).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
