      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_1483004" metaid="metaid_2267" name="Cho is phosphorylated to PCho by CHK dimer" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In the cytosol, choline kinase alpha subunit (CHKA) homodimer, choline kinase beta subunit (CHKB) dimer, or CHKA:CHKB heterodimer phosphorylates choline (Cho) to produce phosphocholine (PCho) (Malito et al. 2006, Gallego-Ortega et al. 2009).</p>
        </notes>
