      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_2046087" metaid="metaid_2268" name="Translocation of tetracosahexaenoyl-CoA to peroxisomes" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The 24-carbon tetracosahexaenoyl-CoA (6,9,12,15,18,21-24:6(n-3) is transported to peroxisomes to undergo a putative single cycle of peroxisomal beta-oxidation, producing Docosahexaenoic Acid (DHA) (Sprecher 2002, Luthria et al. 1996).</p>
        </notes>
