      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9031803" metaid="metaid_2276" name="Maresin-like SPMs translocate from cytosol to extracellular region" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">To produce their pro-resolving effects, maresin-like SPMs (MaR-L1, MaR-L2, 14(S), 21(R/S)-diHDHA and 14(R), 21(R/S)-diHDHA) are released into the exudate of local inflammation sites (Hong et al. 2014). The mechanism of translocation is unknown.</p>
        </notes>
