      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_429730" metaid="metaid_2301" name="PPM1L dephosphorylates multiphospho-CERT1-2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Multiphospho-CERT (ceramide transfer protein) associates with the complex of VAPA/B (VAMP-associated proteins A or B) and PPM1L (protein phosphatase 1-like) in the endoplasmic reticulum membrane (Kawano et al. 2006; Saito et al. 2008; Kumagai and Hanada 2019), enabling PPM1L to catalyze the dephosphorylation of the multiphospho-CERT complex component (Saito et al. 2008; Kumagai and Hanada 2019). This dephosphorylation restores CERT’s ability to bind and transport ceramide.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
