      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_2161613" metaid="metaid_2304" name="PGH2 is degraded to 12S-HHT and MDA by TBXAS1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Thromboxane synthase (TBXAS1) aka CYP5A1 facilitates rearrangement of the PGH2 endoperoxide bridge by a complementary mechanism to prostacyclin synthase, interacting with the C-9 oxygen to promote endoperoxide bond cleavage. The C-11 oxygen radical initiates intramolecular rearrangement, resulting in either the formation of thromboxane A2 (TXA2) or 12-hydroxyheptadecatrienoic acid (12S-HHT) and malonaldehyde (MDA) (Wang et al. 2001).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
