      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2161961" metaid="metaid_2311" name="5,6-EET is hydrolysed to 5,6-DHET by EPHX2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Epoxide hydrolase 2 (EPHX2) hydrolyses 5,6-epoxyeicosatrienoate (5,6-EET) to 5,6-dihydroxyeicosatrienoate (5,6-DHET) (Werner et al. 2002; Gomez et al. 2004). The majority of the EET biological activities are diminished by this hydrolysis.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
