      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_193401" metaid="metaid_2314" name="THCA is conjugated with Coenzyme A (SLC27A2 VLCS)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">THCA (25(R) 3alpha,7alpha,12alpha-trihydroxy-5beta-cholestanoate), coenzyme A, and ATP react to form the CoA conjugate of 25(R) THCA, AMP, and pyrophosphate. This cytosolic reaction is catalyzed by SLC27A2 (VLCS). SLC27A5 (BACS) also catalyzes this reaction; the relative contributions of the two enzymes to de novo bile acid synthesis in vivo are not certain (Mihalik et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
