      <reaction compartment="compartment_161320" fast="false" id="reaction_9840470" metaid="metaid_2331" name="PSAP(195-273) dimer:PE binds and mobilizes ligands" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">By encapsulating phosphatidylethanolamines (PE) of different sizes from the membrane of intralysosomal luminal vesicles (ILV), the Saposin B (PSAP(195-273) dimer can solubilize relatively large lipid ligands from these membranes. Ligands carried by Saposin B include GM1, GM3, Gb3, SM4s, Ga2Cer, and LacCer (Vogel et al., 1991; Wilkening et al., 2000; Ahn et al., 2003; reviewed by Sandhoff and Sandhoff, 2018).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
