      <reaction compartment="compartment_876" fast="false" id="reaction_5333678" metaid="metaid_2336" name="CPNEs bind PL" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Copine 1, 3, 6 and 7 (CPNE1,3,6,7) are a family of calcium-dependent phospholipid-binding proteins thought to be involved in membrane trafficking processes. They contain two C2 domains, one each for the Ca2+- and phospholipid-binding properties (Creutz et al. 1998, Tomsig and Creutz 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
