      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_192137" metaid="metaid_2337" name="THCA is conjugated with Coenzyme A (SLC27A5 BACS)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">THCA (25(R) 3alpha,7alpha,12alpha-trihydroxy-5beta-cholestanoate) , coenzyme A, and ATP react to form the CoA conjugate of 25(R) THCA, AMP, and pyrophosphate. This cytosolic reaction is catalyzed by SLC27A5 (BACS). SLC27A2 (VLCS) also catalyzes this reaction; the relative contributions of the two enzymes to de novo bile acid synthesis in vivo are not certain (Mihalik et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
