      <reaction compartment="compartment_984" fast="false" id="reaction_8963851" metaid="metaid_2350" name="VD3 dissociates from GC" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Vitamin D3 (VD3) is transported to the liver bound to a plasma protein called vitamin D binding protein (GC aka DBP) (Verboven et al. 2002). Before uptake by the liver, VD3 must dissociate from GC.</p>
        </notes>
