      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_977317" metaid="metaid_2353" name="malonyl-CoA is decarboxylated to acetyl-CoA in peroxisome" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Carboxylation of acetyl-CoA and decarboxylation of malonyl-CoA are two processes that can control the amount of the signal transducer malonyl-CoA in the cell. The decarboxylation is catalysed by MCD enzyme in the peroxisomal matrix (Sacksteder et al, 1999).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
