      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_389622" metaid="metaid_2359" name="phytanate + CoA-SH + ATP =&gt; phytanoyl-CoA + AMP + pyrophosphate" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">SLC27A2, also known as VLCS (very long chain acyl-CoA synthetase), associated with the inner surface of the peroxisomal membrane, cayalyzes the reaction of phytanate, CoA-SH, and ATP to form phytanoyl-CoA, AMP, and pyrophosphate (Steinberg et al. 1999).</p>
        </notes>
