      <reaction compartment="compartment_7660" fast="false" id="reaction_2426148" metaid="metaid_2374" name="SREBP1A,1C binds the FASN promoter" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">SREBP1A (SREBF1A) or SREBP1C, together with NF-Y and SP1, bind and transactivate the promoter of the FASN gene (Bennett et al. 1995, Pai et al. 1998, Xiong et al. 2000, Amemiya-Kudo et al. 2002, Shin et al. 2007, Choi et al. 2008, Rome et al. 2008). NF-Y is required for response to cholesterol (Xiong et al. 2000). SREBP1A activates FASN more strongly than does SREBP1C or SREBP2 (Pai et al. 1998, Amemiya-Kudo et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
