      <reaction compartment="compartment_7660" fast="false" id="reaction_2426147" metaid="metaid_2381" name="SREBP1A,1C,2 binds the FDPS promoter" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">SREBP1A/1C/2 (SREBF1A/1C/2), together with NF-Y, bind and transactivate the promoter of the FDPS gene (Ericsson et al. 1996, Pai et al. 1998, Amemiya-Kudo et al. 2002, Reed et al. 2008, Rome et al. 2008, Ishimoto et al. 2010). The binding of NF-Y synergistically enhances the binding of SREBP1 (Ericsson et al. 1996). SREBP1A activates FDPS more strongly than does SREBP2 or SREBP1C (Amemiya-Kudo et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
