      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482629" metaid="metaid_2382" name="2-acyl LPC is hydrolyzed to GPCho by PLA2G4C" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, 2-acyl lysophosphatidylcholine (LPC) is hydrolyzed to glycerophosphocholine (GPCho) by membrane-bound cytosolic phospholipase A2 gamma (PLA2G4C) (Yamashita et al. 2005, Ghomashchi et al. 2010, Yamashita et al. 2009).</p>
        </notes>
