      <reaction compartment="compartment_876" fast="false" id="reaction_1606583" metaid="metaid_2386" name="ASAH2 hydrolyzes ceramide (plasma membrane)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Neutral ceramidase (ASAH2) is an enzyme localised to the plasma membrane that catalyses the hydrolysis of ceramide to sphingosine and free fatty acid (Hwang et al. 2005, Galadari et al. 2006).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
