      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482961" metaid="metaid_2388" name="CDP-Cho and DAG are converted to PC by CEPT1 at the ER membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, choline/ethanolaminephosphotransferase (CEPT1) converts CDP-choline (CDP-Cho) and diacylglycerol (DAG) to phosphatidylcholine (PC) and cytidine monophosphate (CMP) (Wright et al. 2002, Henneberry et al. 1999, Henneberry et al. 2002, Henneberry et al. 2000).</p>
        </notes>
