      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_191366" metaid="metaid_2405" name="Squalene 2,3-epoxide cyclizes, forming lanosterol" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Lanosterol synthase (LSS) catalyzes the cyclization of squalene 2,3-epoxide to lanosterol, a reaction that forms the sterol nucleus (Sung et al. 1995; Van Tamelen et al. 1966). LSS is located on the ER membrane and is active in monomeric form (Ruf et al. 2004).</p>
        </notes>
