      <reaction compartment="compartment_161320" fast="false" id="reaction_9840949" metaid="metaid_2408" name="ARSA removes sulfate from SM3" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Sulfated sphingoglycolipid GM3 (SM3, sulfated LacCer, dihexosyl sulfatide) is desulfated by arylsulfatase A (ARSA) to lactosylceramide (LacCer). In metachromatic leukodystrophy (MLD, MIM:250100), SM3 and other sulfatides accumulate, usually because of ARSA deficiency (Philppart et al., 1971; Whitfield et al., 2001).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
