      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_2161619" metaid="metaid_2417" name="PGI2 is hydrolysed to 6k-PGF1a" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The ring in prostaglandin I2 (PGI2) aka prostacyclin is highly labile and rapidly hydolyses to form the stable but biologically inactive 6-keto-prostaglandin F1alpha (6k-PGF1a) (Wada et al. 2004). PGI2 and 6k-PGF1a are often used interchangeably in the literature.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
