      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_9915997" metaid="metaid_2420" name="Arachidonate is epoxidated to 14,15-EET by CYP(5)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Several cytochrome P450s (CYPs) convert arachidonate to 14,15-epoxyeicosatrienoate (14,15-EET). The CYPs and their references are: CYP1A1, CYP1A2, CYP1B1 (Choudhary et al. 2004); CYP2C8, CYP2C9 (Rifkind et al. 1995); CYP2C19 (Bylund et al. 1998, Rifkind et al. 1995); CYP2J2 (Wu et al. 1996).</p>
        </notes>
