      <reaction compartment="compartment_17951" fast="false" id="reaction_6787811" metaid="metaid_2424" name="HAO2 tetramer oxidises 2OH-PALM" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Fatty acids can be metabolised by two distinct pathways; alpha- and beta-oxidation. Peroxisomal hydroxyacid oxidase 2 (HAO2) is thought to take part in alpha-oxidation of long chain fatty acids such as 2-hydroxypalmitate (2OH-PALM). HAO2 functions as a homotetramer and is highly expressed in liver and kidney (Jones et al. 2000).</p>
        </notes>
