      <reaction compartment="compartment_5460" fast="false" id="reaction_5696004" metaid="metaid_2425" name="ACSF2 ligates CoA-SH to MCFA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Acyl-coenzyme A synthetases (ACSs) catalyse the activation of fatty acids by thioesterification to CoA, the fundamental initial reaction in fatty acid metabolism. Mitochondrial acyl-CoA synthetase family member 2 (ACSF2) preferentially ligates CoA-SH to medium-chain fatty acids (MCFA), around C8 in length (Watkins et al. 2007).</p>
        </notes>
