      <reaction compartment="compartment_984" fast="false" id="reaction_8963872" metaid="metaid_2432" name="VD3 translocates from ER membrane to extracellular region" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Vitamin D metabolites such as VD3 are lipophilic and must be transported in the circulation bound to plasma proteins. VD3 translocates to the extracellular region where it binds GC, a vitamin D binding protein (Verboven et al. 2002).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
