      <reaction compartment="compartment_17906" fast="false" id="reaction_1482695" metaid="metaid_2441" name="G3P is acylated to 1-acyl LPA by GPAM/GPAT2 (OM)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Glycerol-3-phosphate (G3P) is acylated to 1-acyl lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) by the enzymes glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase 1 (GPAT, also known as GPAM) and glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase 2 (GPAT2), at the outer mitochondrial (OM) membrane (Shindou and Shimizu 2009, Chen et al. 2008, Takeuchi and Reue 2009).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
