      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_8848215" metaid="metaid_2462" name="ACAT2 condenses 2 Ac-CoA to form ACA-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Three human enzymes, two mitochondrial and one cytosolic, catalyze the interconversion of acetyl-CoA and acetoacetyl-CoA. The cytosolic form, acetyl-CoA acetyltransferase tetramer (ACAT2 tetramer) (Song et al. 1994), catalyses the condensation of two acetyl-CoA (Ac-CoA) molecules to form acetoacetyl-CoA (ACA-CoA). This is the first step in the biosynthesis of cholesterol (Fukao et al. 1997).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
