      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_5695957" metaid="metaid_2495" name="ACSBG1,2 ligates CoA-SH to VLCFA, forming VLCFA-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Long-chain fatty acid-CoA ligases 1 and 2 (ACSBG1 and 2) are capable of activating very long-chain fatty acids (VLCFA) and are thought to play a role in fatty acid metabolism in the brain (ACSBG1 and 2) (Steinberg et al. 2000, Pei et al. 2003), and testes (ACSBG2) (Pei et al. 2006).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
