      <reaction compartment="compartment_17963" fast="false" id="reaction_9846305" metaid="metaid_2502" name="ST6GALNAC5,6 transfer Neu5Ac to GM1b" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Alpha-2,6-sialyltransferases 5 and 6 (ST6GALNAC5,6) transfer a sialic acid (Neu5Ac) moiety to the terminal N-acetylgalactosaminyl (GalNAc) residue of ganglioside GM1b to produce ganglioside GD1alpha (GD1α). Neu5Ac is added to GalNAc-R via an alpha-2,6 linkage (Ikehara et al. 1999, Tsuchida et al. 2003). To date, the specific function of α-series gangliosides is poorly understood.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
