      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1483081" metaid="metaid_2503" name="PCho and CTP are condensed to CDP-Cho by PCYT1 dimer" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, active membrane-bound choline-phosphate cytidylyltransferase A (PCYT1A) or B (PCYT1B) homodimer condenses phosphocholine (PCho) and cytidine triphosphate (CTP) to produce CDP-choline (CDP-Cho) (Lykidis et al. 1998).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
