      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_266050" metaid="metaid_2517" name="LTA4 is converted to LTC4 by LTC4S" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Leukotriene A4 conjugates with reduced glutathione (GSH) to produce leukotriene C4 (LTC4). This conjugation is mediated by the homodimeric, perinuclear membrane-bound enzyme leukotriene C4 synthase (LTC4S) (Lam et al. 1994, Welsch et al. 1994). LTC4S differs from cytosolic and microsomal GSH-S-transferases by having a very narrow substrate specificity and the inability to conjugate xenobiotics.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
