      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_428696" metaid="metaid_2525" name="PLPP1,2,3 dephosphorylate cytosolic sphingosine-1-phosphate" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Phospholipid phosphatases 1 (PLPP1, PPAP2A, LPP1), 2 (PLPP2, LPP2, PPAP2C), and 3 (PLPP3, LPP3, PPAP2B) associated with the plasma membrane catalyze the hydrolysis of cytosolic sphingosine 1-phosphate to form sphingosine and orthophosphate (Roberts et al. 1998). PLPPs have roles in angiogenesis and cancer (reviewed by Tang et al., 2015; Tang and Brindley, 2020).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
