      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1483089" metaid="metaid_2532" name="PE is converted to PS by PTDSS2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidylserine synthase 2 (PTDSS2) converts phosphatidylethanolamine (PE) into phosphatidylserine (PS) by facilitating the exchange of L-Serine (L-Ser) with the ethanolamine (ETA) head group (Saito et al. 1998, Tomohiro et al. 2009).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
