      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9025957" metaid="metaid_2535" name="ALOX12:Fe2+ oxidises DPAn-6 to 14(S)-HDPAn-6" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The main product of ω-6 docosapentaenoic acid (DPAn-6) oxygenation by 12-lipoxygenase (ALOX12:Fe2+) is 14(S)-hydroxy-DPAn-6 (14(S)-HDPAn-6) (Dangi et al. 2009, 2010, Dobson et al. 2013). The final product is produced via a hydroperoxy intermediate, which is then reduced to the corresponding hydroxy compound (these details not described here and also, the human enzymes involved in these reactions are unknown). This DPAn-6 product is analogous in structure and action to DHA (docosahexaenoic acid)-derived resolvins (Dangi et al. 2010).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
