      <reaction compartment="compartment_5460" fast="false" id="reaction_73912" metaid="metaid_2544" name="acetoacetic acid + NADH + H+ &lt;=&gt; beta-hydroxybutyrate + NAD+" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">D-beta-hydroxybutyrate dehydrogenase tetramer (BDH1) in the mitochondrial matris catalyzes the reversible reaction of acetoacetate with NADH + H+ to form D-beta hydroxybutyrate and NAD+ (Marks et al. 1992).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
