      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_8849969" metaid="metaid_2558" name="PI(4,5)P2, PI(3,4)P2 and PI(3,4,5)P3 are dephosphorylated to PI5P, PI3P and PI(3,4)P by INPP5F at the endosome membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Characterization of human INPP5F (SAC2) identified that it is a 4-phosphatase with highest activity against PI(4,5)P2, PI(3,4)P2, and PI(3,4,5)P3, generating PI(5)P, PI(3)P and PI(3,5)P2 respectively (Nakatsu et al. 2015, Hsu et al. 2015). Inpp5f -/- mice have elevated level of PIP3 and exhibit accentuated cardiac hypertrophy as measured by heart size, myocyte size and gene expression (Zhu et al. 2009).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
