      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9705714" metaid="metaid_2569" name="SRD5A3 dehydrogenates TEST to DHTEST" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The conversion of testosterone (TEST) to the most potent androgen, 5-alpha-dihydrotestosterone (DHTEST), is catalyzed by microsomal 5alpha-steroid reductase 3 (SRD5A3) (Uemura et al. 2008). SRD5A3 is expressed in the prostate and other androgen target sites. Corticotropin (Adrenocorticotropic hormone, ACTH) acts through melanocortin receptor type 2 (MC2R) to stimulate steroidogenesis, increasing the production of androgens (McKenna et al. 1997).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
