      <reaction compartment="compartment_70616" fast="false" id="reaction_1482775" metaid="metaid_2571" name="MLCL is acylated to CL by HADH (IM)" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the inner mitochondrial membrane (IM), the trifunctional enzyme HADH (3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase), an octamer of four alpha (HADHA) and four beta (HADHB) subunits, acylates monolysocardiolipin (MLCL) to cardiolipin (CL) (Taylor and Hatch 2009).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
