      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2161662" metaid="metaid_2582" name="PGD2/E2/F2a is oxidised to 15k-PGD2/E2/F2a by HPGD" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">15-Hydroxyprostaglandin dehydrogenase (HPGD) oxidises prostaglandins D2 (PGD2), E2 (PGE2), and F2alpha (PGF2a) to 15-keto-prostaglandin D2 (15k-PGD2), E2 (15k-PGE2), and F2alpha (15k-PGF2a) respectively (Cho et al. 2006). This reaction is inferred from rabbits (Bergholte and Okita 1986).</p>
        </notes>
