      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2309779" metaid="metaid_2591" name="PTGS2 dimer binds PTGS2 inhibitors" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">While closely similar, PTGS1 and 2 differ sufficiently in the structures of their active sites so that the latter enzyme selectively binds and is inhibited by PTGS2 inhibitors (benzquinamide, carprofen, celecoxib, etodolac, etoricoxib, lumiracoxib, rofecoxib, valdecoxib) (Luong et al. 1996; Smith et al. 2000; Dong et al. 2011).</p>
        </notes>
