      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_1483107" metaid="metaid_2594" name="GPETA is hydrolyzed to ETA and G3P by GPCPD1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In the cytosol, glycerophosphocholine phosphodiesterase (GPCPD1, also known as GDE5) hydrolyzes glycerophosphoethanolamine (GPETA) to produce ethanolamine (ETA) and glycerol-3-phosphate (G3P). This event has been inferred from mice. GPCPD1 has also been characterized in humans (Ota et al. 2004).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
