      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_2046084" metaid="metaid_2598" name="Desaturation of alpha-linoleoyl-CoA to Stearidonoyl-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Alpha-linoloyl-CoA is converted to Stearidonoyl-CoA (SDA, 6,9,12,15-18:3(n-3)) by delta-6-destaurase (fatty acid desaturase-2, FADS2). FADS2 uses the cytochrome b5 system to add a double bond at position 6. This is the rate limiting step in alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) metabolism (Horrobin 1993).</p>
        </notes>
