      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2161948" metaid="metaid_2606" name="Arachidonate  is converted to 12-oxoETE by ALOX12" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Arachidonate 12-lipoxygenase, 12S-type (ALOX12) catalyses the formation of 12-oxo-eicosatetraenoic acid (12-oxoETE) from arachidonic acid. This conversion has been observed when normal human epidermis is exposed to arachidonate and with the purified recombinant enzyme in vitro (Anton and Vila 2000).</p>
        </notes>
