      <reaction compartment="compartment_17957" fast="false" id="reaction_140359" metaid="metaid_2610" name="PGG2 is reduced to PGH2 by PTGS1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Prostaglandin G/H synthase 1 (PTGS1) exhibits a dual catalytic activity, a cyclooxygenase and a peroxidase. The peroxidase function converts prostaglandin G2 (PGG2) to prostaglandin H2 (PGH2) via a two-electron reduction (Hamberg et al. 1973, Hla and Neilson 1992, Swinney et al. 1997, Barnett et al. 1994).</p>
        </notes>
