      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482571" metaid="metaid_2615" name="1-acyl LPE is hydrolyzed to GPETA by PLA2G4C" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, membrane-bound cytosolic phospholipase A2 gamma (PLA2G4C) hydrolyzes 1-acyl lysophosphatidylethanolamine (LPE) to produce glycerophosphoethanolamine (GPETA) (Yamashita et al. 2005, Yamashita et al. 2009).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
