      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9027628" metaid="metaid_2618" name="ALOX5 oxidises EPA to 5-HEPE" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In human neutrophils, 5-lipoxygenase (ALOX5) can mediate the lipoxygenation of eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) to 5-hydroxy-eicosapentaenoic acid (5-HEPE) (Cipollina et al. 2014, Powell et al. 1995). Neutrophils treated with an ALOX5 inhibitor completely suppressed the formation of 5-oxo-EPA and its hydroxy precursor 5-HEPE, demonstrating that ALOX5 mediates the first step in 5-oxo-EPA biosynthesis (Cipollina et al. 2014).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
