      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_428664" metaid="metaid_2628" name="SGPP1,2 dephosphorylate sphingoid-1-phosphates" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">SGPP1 and 2 (sphingosine-1-phosphate phosphatase 1 and 2) enzymes associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane catalyze the hydrolysis of cytosolic sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P), dihydro-S1P, and phyto-S1P. to form sphinganine (dihydrosphingosine, phytosphingosine) and orthophosphate. Availability of sphingoids versus sphingoid-1-phosphates has direct influence on all processes involving ceramides (Johnson et al. 2003; Ogawa et al. 2003; Giussani et al., 2006).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
