      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_548843" metaid="metaid_2631" name="ACSL3,4 ligate CoA to AA to form AA-CoA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Acyl-CoA synthetase long-chain family member 4 (ACSL4) associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane catalyses the conjugation of arachidonate (AA) with CoA to form arachidonyl-CoA (AA-CoA) (Longo et al. 2003, Meloni et al. 2003). By similarity, ACSL3 can also preferentially conjugate CoA on to AA (Yao and Ye 2008). These enzymes are involved in the activation of long-chain fatty acids for both synthesis of cellular lipids, and degradation via beta-oxidation.</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
