      <reaction compartment="compartment_5460" fast="false" id="reaction_193997" metaid="metaid_2635" name="CYP11B1 oxidises 11DCORT" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Cytochrome P450 11B1, mitochondrial (CYP11B1) usually hydroxylates 11-deoxycortisol (11DCORT) to form cortisol (CORT). CYP11B1 is associated with the inner mitochondrial membrane. Corticotropin (Adrenocorticotropic hormone, ACTH) acts through the ACTH receptor, melanocortin receptor type 2 (MC2R) to stimulate steroidogenesis, increasing the production of androgens (McKenna et al, 1997).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
