      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_193073" metaid="metaid_2636" name="HSD2B1 dimer, HSD3B2 dimer isomerise DHA to ANDST" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In this two-step reaction catalyzed by 3beta-HSD associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane, the 3-hydroxyl group of DHA is oxidized to a keto group and the double bond in the steroid nucleus is then isomerized from the five to the 4 position. Corticotropin (Adrenocorticotropic hormone, ACTH) acts through the ACTH receptor called melanocortin receptor type 2 (MC2R) to stimulate steroidogenesis, increasing the production of androgens (McKenna et al, 1997).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
