      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_549112" metaid="metaid_2646" name="G3P is acylated to 1-acyl LPA by AGPAT6" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Glycerol-3-phosphate (G3P) is acylated to 1-acyl lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) by the enzymes glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase 4 (AGPAT6) at the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane (Cao et al., 2006; Chen et al., 2008).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
