      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9020271" metaid="metaid_2653" name="GPX4-2 reduces 17(R)-Hp-DHA to 17(R)-HDHA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Cytosolic phospholipid hydroperoxide glutathione peroxidase (GPX4 isoform 2, GPX4-2) (Yagi et al. 1996) is a likely candidate for the reduction of organic hydroperoxides such as 17(R)-hydroperoxy-docosahexaenoic acid (17(R)-Hp-DHA) to 17(R)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (17(R)-HDHA) (Han et al. 2013) using glutathione (GSH) as an electron donor (Brigelius-Flohe and Maiorino 2013). 17(R)-HDHA can then be transformed into 17(R)-D-resolvins and a 17-oxo electrophilic product 17-oxo-DHA (Groeger et al. 2010).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
