      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_2161951" metaid="metaid_2654" name="Arachidonate is oxidised to 15R-HETE by Acetyl-PTGS2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Aspirin acetylates the cyclooxygenase, prostaglandin G/H synthase 2 (PTGS2) aka COX2. The acetylated PTGS2 triggers the formation of 15R-hydroxyeicosatetraenoate (15R-HETE) from arachidonate (Claria and Serhan 1995).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
