      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482868" metaid="metaid_2656" name="PI is hydrolyzed to 1-acyl LPI by PLA2[12]" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidylinositol (PI) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by membrane-associated phospholipase A2 gamma 2A (PLA2G2A) (Singer et al. 2002) or by cytosolic phospholipase A2 gamma (PLA2G4C) (Ghomashchi et al. 2010), to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidylinositol (LPI).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
