      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482889" metaid="metaid_2657" name="DAG is acylated to TAG by DGAT1/2" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, diacylglycerol (DAG) is acylated and forms triacylglycerol (TAG) by the action of diacylglycerol O-acyltransferase 1 (DGAT1) tetramer or by diacylglycerol O-acyltransferase 2 (DGAT2) (Wakimoto et al. 2003, Oelkers et al. 1998, Cases et al. 2001).</p>
        </notes>
