      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9020282" metaid="metaid_2663" name="ALOX5 oxidises 17(S)-HDHA to 7(S)-Hp-17(S)-HDHA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Lipoxygenase 5 (ALOX5) can oxidise 17(S)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (17(S)-HDHA) into two hydroperoxy intermediates in human polymorphonuclear leukocytes (PMNs) (Serhan et al. 2002). The formation of 7(S)-hydroperoxy-17(S)-hydroxydocosahexaenoic acid (7(S)-Hp-17(S)-HDHA) is decribed here.</p>
        </notes>
