      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_8963913" metaid="metaid_2670" name="1,25(OH)2D translocates from cytosol to nucleoplasm" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The biologically active form of vitamin D, 1-alpha, 25-dihydroxyvitamin D (1,25(OH)2D), can be transported to any target tissue where it enters the nucleoplasm to interact with vitamin D receptor (VDR) to exert its effects. The mechanism of translocation from cytosol to nucleoplasm is unknown (see review for general description - Christakos et al. 2016).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
