      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_200423" metaid="metaid_2675" name="pAMPK inactivates ACACB, inhibiting malonyl-CoA synthesis" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Acetyl-CoA carboxylase 2 (ACACB, ACC2) is involved in the regulation of mitochondrial fatty acid oxidation through the inhibition of carnitine palmitoyltransferase 1 by its product malonyl-CoA. Phosphorylated AMPK inactivates ACACB in muscle cells by phosphorylation. This results in decreased levels of malonyl CoA, contributing to the homeostasis of mitochondrial beta oxidation (Ruderman and Prentki 2004).</p>
        </notes>
