      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9024890" metaid="metaid_2679" name="LTA4H:Zn2+ hydrolyses 16S,17S-epoxy-DHA to (N)PD1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Leukotriene A4 hydrolase (LTA4H) is a monomeric, soluble enzyme that uses a Zn2+ cofactor to catalyse the hydrolysis of the allylic epoxide leukotriene A4 (LTA4) (McGee and Fitzpatrick 1985). When produced in neural tissue, where it affords potent tissue protective actions, this docsanoid is called neuroprotectin D1 (NPD1).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
