      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_9947203" metaid="metaid_2680" name="MSMO1 oxidizes 4,4-diMe-5-cholest-8-en-3-ol to 4a-carboxy-4b-me-5a-cholest-8-en-3b-ol" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">MSMO1 (Methylsterol monooxygenase 1), associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane, oxidizes 4,4-diMe5-cholest-8-en-3-ol to 4a-carboxy-4b-me-5a-cholest-8-en-3beta-ol. Evidence for this function of human MSMO1 protein is indirect, coming from studies of steroid synthesis intermediates accumulated in patients with defects in the enzyme (He et al. 2011).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
