      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_191299" metaid="metaid_2682" name="Squalene is oxidized to its epoxide" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Squalene monooxygenase (squalene epoxidase, SE) is located on the endoplamic reticulum. It catalyzes the oxidation of squalene (SQNE) to squalene 2,3-epoxide (SQNX) (Laden et al. 2000).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
