      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9026911" metaid="metaid_2687" name="LTC4S trimer transfers GSH to 7S(8)-epoxy-17(S)-HDHA to form RCTR1" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Just as the addition of glutathione (GSH) to an allylic epoxide is governed by glutathione S-transferase enzymes in the biosynthesis of MCTR (Dalli et al. 2016), 7S(8)-epoxy-17(S)-hydroxy-docosahexaenoic acid (7S(8)-epoxy-17(S)-HDHA) may presumably be conjugated with GSH by trimeric leukotriene C4 synthase (LTC4S trimer) to form resolvin conjugate in tissue regeneration 1 (RCTR1, 8-glutathionyl, 7,17-dihydroxy-docosahexaenoic acid) (Dalli et al. 2015).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
