      <reaction compartment="compartment_171062" fast="false" id="reaction_1676162" metaid="metaid_2701" name="PI(3,4)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI3P by INPP4A/B at the early endosome membrane" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the early endosome membrane, type I (INPP4A) (Norris et al. 1995, Ivetac et al. 2005) and type II inositol-3,4-bisphosphate 4-phosphatase (INPP4B) (Norris et al. 1997) colocalise with early and recycling endosomes through their C2 domains which bind to the phosphatidylinositol 3,4-bisphosphate (PI(3,4)P2) present in these membranes. It is here that phosphatidylinositol 3,4-bisphosphate (PI(3,4)P2) is dephosphorylated by INPP4A/B to phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate (PI3P).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
