      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2161791" metaid="metaid_2711" name="15S-HpETE is reduced to 15S-HETE by GPX1/2/4" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Glutathione peroxidases (GPXs) in human platelets (either GPX1, GPX2, or GPX4 are present in the cytosol) are involved in reducing 15S-hydroperoxyeicosatetraenoic acid (15S-HpETE) to 15S-hydroxyeicosatetraenoic acid (15S-HETE) (Hill et al. 1989).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
