      <reaction compartment="compartment_161320" fast="false" id="reaction_350158" metaid="metaid_2712" name="LGMN hydrolyzes GC, releasing CUBN and 25(OH)D" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In the acidic environment of the lysosome, LGMN (legumain asparagine-specific endoprotease) hydrolyzes the GC (vitamin D-binding protein) component of the CUBN:GC:25(OH)D complex, releasing cubilin (CUBN) and 25(OH)D (25-hydroxyvitamin D, calcidiol) (Nykjaer et al. 1999).</p>
        </notes>
