      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_9018859" metaid="metaid_2720" name="ALOX5 oxidises 5(S)-Hp-18(S)-HEPE to 5S,6S-epoxy-18(S)-HEPE" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In neutrophils, 5-lipoxygenase (ALOX5) can mediate the insertion of molecular oxygen into 5(S)-hydroperoxy-18(S)-hydroxyeicosapentaenoic acid (5(S)-Hp-18(S)-HEPE) to form 5S,6S-epoxy-18(S)-HEPE which is essential for 18(S)-resolvin E1 biosynthesis (Tjonahen et al. 2006, Oh et al. 2012).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
