      <reaction compartment="compartment_7660" fast="false" id="reaction_879724" metaid="metaid_2722" name="Expression of PPARA" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The PPARA gene is transcribed to yield mRNA and the mRNA is translated to yield protein. As inferred from mouse, BMAL1:CLOCK (ARNTL:CLOCK) heterodimers bind E-box elements in the second intron of the PPARA gene and activate transcription of PPARA.</p>
        </notes>
