      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_1482656" metaid="metaid_2735" name="PA is hydrolysed to 1-acyl LPA by PLA2[1]" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidic acid (PA) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by phospholipase A2 alpha/beta/delta/zeta (PLA2G4A/B/D/F) to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) (Ghomashchi et al. 2010).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
