      <reaction compartment="compartment_12045" fast="false" id="reaction_1482545" metaid="metaid_2751" name="2-acyl LPE is hydrolyzed to GPETA by PLA2G4C" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, membrane-bound cytosolic phospholipase A2 gamma (PLA2G4C) hydrolyzes 2-acyl lysophosphatidylethanolamine (LPE) to produce glycerophosphoethanolamine (GPETA) (Yamashita et al. 2005, Yamashita et al. 2009).</p>
        </notes>
