      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_2161776" metaid="metaid_2753" name="5S-HETE is oxidised to 5-oxoETE by 5-HEDH" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Current literature suggests that 5S-hydroxy-eicosatetraenoic acid (5S-HETE) itself does not appear to play a significant role in biological signalling. However, it can be further oxidised by a 5-hydroxy-eicosatetraenoic acid dehydrogenase (5-HEDH) to form the bioactive 5-oxo-eicosatetraenoic acid (5-oxoETE, also known as 5-KETE. While the gene has not yet been cloned, the biophysical properties of the human enzyme have been well characterised (Powell et al. 1992).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
