      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_469659" metaid="metaid_2769" name="SRD5A1 dehydrogenates TEST to DHTEST" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The conversion of testosterone to the most potent androgen, 5-alpha-dihydrotestosterone (DHTEST), is catalyzed by microsomal 5alpha-steroid reductase 1 (SRD5A1) (Andersson and Russell 1990). SRD5A1 is expressed in the prostate and other androgen target sites. Corticotropin (Adrenocorticotropic hormone, ACTH) acts through melanocortin receptor type 2 (MC2R) to stimulate steroidogenesis, increasing the production of androgens (McKenna et al. 1997).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
